onment's allowed hosts, normally within seconds. Files, running processes and this conversation stay as they are. The target's variables are NOT set now: they are set from the next restart of Claude on this machine. Its setup script does NOT run now or at a restart: it runs only if the machine is replaced. Calling this tool IS the request for permission: the user is shown an approval prompt with the target's name and network, and must approve in every permission mode. So do not ask the user in chat first. Use it to move to an environment that get_environment lists in `saved_for_session_repositories`, or when the user asked to move this session. First call get_environment with the target's environment_id, then copy its `switch_statement` unchanged into `switch_statement`: the call is refused, changing nothing, if it does not match the target as it is when the user approves. Environments with unrestricted network access or a wildcard host are refused: start a new session on those instead. Network secrets saved on the target are sent to their hosts once this session has moved, and those saved on the current environment stop being used, which can take up to an hour; the approval prompt lists the hosts of both. If the user declines, or the call is refused, do not ask again in chat; carry on in this environment and say what remains blocked.", "name": "mcp__claude-code-remote__switch_environment", "schema": {"description": "Move THIS session onto another existing cloud environment the user can already use, without replacing this machine. Only the session's network changes: requests through the session's HTTPS proxy follow the target environment's allowed hosts, normally within seconds. Files, running processes and this conversation stay as they are. The target's variables are NOT set now: they are set from the next restart of Claude on this machine. Its setup script does NOT run now or at a restart: it runs only if the machine is replaced. Calling this tool IS the request 